  "answer": "The available evidence does not establish a **guaranteed** calendar day for Microsoft Teams integration to become generally available. The official roadmap [NL-014#NL-014-S04] lists a **target release date of November 24, 2026** for v2.11.0 (Microsoft Teams Connector), and [NL-014#NL-014-S07] describes it as \"Planned for Q4 2026\" with a restricted pilot beginning in October 2026. However, [NL-014#NL-014-S09] explicitly states that engineering risks (resource constraints, Microsoft Graph API changes) mean \"feature timelines may slip.\" Additionally, [NL-015#NL-015-S06] records the CTO stating the integration \"will stay in the design phase for Q4, with development slated for early 2027,\" contradicting the November 24, 2026 target. [NL-023#NL-023-S04] labels the claim that it is \"almost ready\" as a \"significant sales overclaim,\" confirming that the official status is \"in design / planned for Q4 2026\" and not generally available. Because the evidence contains a target date but explicitly frames it as non-guaranteed and includes conflicting internal timelines, there is no guaranteed calendar day in the evidence.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: abstain\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
